h1 Week of Nov 11: Playdate tools and Vermont budget prefills

p Most of my public work this week was Playdate tooling, plus a few changes to the Vermont education budget review.

p Playdate:

ul
  li Two merged pull requests on #[a(href='https://github.com/jamesjnadeau/playdate-performance-simulator') playdate-performance-simulator] (Nov 15). One runs Lua and C games in the browser through WebAssembly. The other adds reopening the last game, gamepad, touch and tilt input, and a WASM size budget.
  li A pure-Rust Thumb-2 and FPv5 interpreter, pdsim-thumb, with its block traces compared against Unicorn in CI.
  li A public repo, #[a(href='https://github.com/jamesjnadeau/playdate-lua-abuse') playdate-lua-abuse] (Nov 15). It is a test game that tries to stress the hardware and drop frames, with a check script that runs modes for garbage, overdraw, sprites, disk, hot loops and auto-cycling.
  li A sailing sim HUD on #[a(href='https://github.com/jamesjnadeau/playdate-sailing-sim/pull/5') PR 5 of playdate-sailing-sim] (merged Nov 16). The wind dial shows true wind and shades the no-go wedge, and helm mode shows the rudder position.

p Vermont budget review, #[a(href='https://github.com/jamesjnadeau/vt-education-budget-review') vt-education-budget-review]:

ul
  li Three pull requests merged on Nov 14 (#[a(href='https://github.com/jamesjnadeau/vt-education-budget-review/pull/60') 60], #[a(href='https://github.com/jamesjnadeau/vt-education-budget-review/pull/61') 61], #[a(href='https://github.com/jamesjnadeau/vt-education-budget-review/pull/62') 62]). The model form now prefills from AOE town-of-residence band sums, every AOE district appears in the model picker, and the Act 127 transition is modeled with the Act 84 decrease prefilled.
  li Commits on Nov 16 flag lower-limit estimates with their own checkbox and tag, and offer suggestions for blank model fields, marked as suggestions when used.
